        "text": " \\\\\n\\end{xltabular}\n\n\\section{Appendix II: Software Design Details}\n\\label"
      }, {
        "text": "{sec:software-design}\nThe simulation data modeling was implemented using the Kotlin Multiplatform \\autocite{"
      }, {
        "text": "noauthor_kotlin_nodate} toolset, popular for developing applications which compile for multiple runtimes. The simulation"
      }, {
        "text": " visualization was created with the corresponding UI framework, Kotlin Compose \\autocite{noauthor_get_nodate}."
      }, {
        "text": " The simulation was built and packaged using Gradle \\autocite{noauthor_gradle_2025}, developed"
      }, {
        "text": " using the IntelliJ IDEA: Ultimate Edition\n\\autocite{noauthor_leading_nodate}, and tested on"
      }, {
        "text": " a 2024 Apple Mac mini with an Apple M4 CPU and 24 gigabytes of RAM."
      }, {
        "text": " While the simulation application has been made available for both macOS and Windows distributions, it has not yet been tested on Windows. "
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nKinetics were numerically solved using a first-order differential equations solver from the Apache Maths Commons Java library \\autoc"
      }, {
        "text": "ite{noauthor_math_nodate}. It was configured to use the Dormand-Prince 853"
      }, {
        "text": " integrator with default parameters \\autocite{noauthor_dormandprince853integrator_nodate"
      }, {
        "text": "}. Optimization of these parameters would likely improve the accuracy of simulation performance. This is a candidate for future work.\n\nAll"
      }, {
        "text": " code and build artifacts from this work are publicly available on GitHub: \\\\\n\\url{https://github.com/jsharp"
      }, {
        "text": "4/PeanutsMetabolismSimulator}\n\nClaude Code was used via a command-line terminal during project development. See"
      }, {
        "text": " \\nameref{sec:ai}.\n\n\\section{Appendix III: A.I. Usage}\n\\label"
      }, {
        "text": "{sec:ai}\nCommercially available A.I. tools were used to assist with the construction of this"
      }, {
        "text": " simulation and for formatting aspects of this paper. All suggested output was verified by this author. All ideas within the paper and"
      }, {
        "text": " in simulation data design are cited or the original work of this author.\n\nClaude Code was used for code refactoring,"
      }, {
        "text": " assistance with triaging issues within the application, formatting Kotlin Compose visuals, and constructing drafts of tables from information already manually embedded"
      }, {
        "text": " in the code. \n\nGoogle AI Studio was used to extract numerical values, units, equations, and abbreviations from publications"
      }, {
        "text": " into formats usable within Kotlin code, to improve the formatting of LaTeX markup, and to search for the location of known content within publications"
      }, {
        "text": ". It was also used for code debugging assistance and written grammar/proofreading.\n\nArchives of all conversations with Claude Code and AI Studio"
      }, {
        "text": " are available at: \\\\\n\\url{https://github.com/jsharp4/PeanutsMetabolismSimulator"
